Level1 Fixed Color Stroke =
SWITCH (
    MAX ( 'MappedParameter'[Category] ),
    "PLACEHOLDER_VALUE_1", "#FCFCFD",
    BLANK () // falls back to level1DefaultStrokeColor in the spec -- see below
)
// Level1's field parameter is 'MappedParameter'[Category] -- see
// level-fixed-color-fill.dax for the full writeup (same field parameter,
// same MAX-not-SELECTEDVALUE reasoning, same "one of three, copy per
// level with a unique measure name and the level's own field parameter"
// note -- Level2/Level3 use 'MappedParameterTwo'[Category2]/
// 'MappedParameterThree'[Category3] respectively). This file exists
// separately from the fill version because
// fill and stroke are independent per-category overrides, each with its
// own fallback param (level1DefaultFillColor vs level1DefaultStrokeColor)
// -- most of the time you won't need this at all, since every level's
// default stroke color already matches the shared background (#182231),
// giving every circle a clean, uniform outline. Use this measure only if
// specific categories need to stand out with a distinct stroke (e.g.
// flagging an outlier), leaving BLANK() for everything else.
//
// Bind to Level1ColorOverrideBorder (rename for this visual -- the spec
// maps it to the internal Level1StrokeOverride role). Unlike the older
// ColorOverrideBorder fields on the aster plot and waffle chart, this
// field is new to this visual and was never bound live before it existed
// -- so it uses "Stroke," not "Border," in its own raw field name from
// the start, per docs/design-system.md's naming convention.
